# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_render.py" "CO-CHANGE RENDER GATE: PASS" "co-change render line (empirical coupling in the PR comment)" "co-change render line: the empirical 'you touched A; historically B comes with it' coupling rendered in the PR comment, with every PO-locked principle. ADDITIVE -- shown ONLY for a strong base-rate-corrected (lift) positive coupling, and it makes a CLEAR PR comment (a co-signal, like shared_foundation); shows the directional CONFIDENCE (73%) AND the LIFT (4.5x more than chance) -- never an average, and NEVER the raw support count (the N-of-M co-occurrence count is DROPPED under the moat rule raw counts banned coverage percent OK; the percent + the lift carry the signal, gate 184 locks the absence). JUDGMENT-NOT-VERDICT (Advisory / Check whether) and it does NOT change the verdict (a clear PR stays clear/success). UNKNOWN != CLEAR: it NEVER claims '0% / not coupled = safe' -- a brand-new or just-split file with no history is rendered 'not evaluated', NOT 'no coupling'. FORK-SAFE: a fork PR NEVER shows co-change (the partner files are base-repo paths the external contributor must not see -- the is_fork redaction returns before the co-change section). content-free (paths + a normalized % + lift, no raw count). Proven on the real render_pr_check" "co-change render: the empirical coupling line is additive (confidence + lift, never an average, no raw count), advisory (not a verdict), unknown-not-0% (a no-history file is 'not evaluated', never 'safe'), and fork-redacted; content-free" 24
